  "summary": {
    "en": "Ecuador is experiencing intensified confrontations as the U.S. military conducts its first land operation against cartels while prison gangs fought inside a prison, killing at least 68 inmates. Journalist Tomás Beltrán Conforme was shot dead despite being under witness protection, and former president's son was charged with cocaine trafficking alongside four others. A Polish drug kingpin was arrested in Ecuador and a major cocaine and weapons trafficking ring was busted in New York, while Luisa González was denied habeas corpus by an Ecuadorian court. A magnitude 4.7 earthquake struck off Ecuador with no tsunami warning, and there were 2 battle-related deaths in 2019, according to UCDP.",
